    "type": "Coding",
    "question": "Write a function `maxSubarraySum(nums, k)` that returns the maximum sum of any contiguous subarray of size `k`.",
    "hints": [
      "Compute initial window sum of first k elements, then slide window by adding incoming and subtracting outgoing element."
    ],
    "solution": "function maxSubarraySum(nums, k) {\n  if (!nums || nums.length < k) return 0;\n  let windowSum = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) windowSum += nums[i];\n  let maxSum = windowSum;\n  for (let i = k; i < nums.length; i++) {\n    windowSum += nums[i] - nums[i - k];\n    maxSum = Math.max(maxSum, windowSum);\n  }\n  return maxSum;\n}",
    "explanation": "Sliding window computes consecutive subarray sums in O(1) per step, reducing brute force O(n*k) to O(n).",
